{"nodes": [{"id": "memories_jira_slack_integration_infrastructure_polling_architecture", "label": "Purely Polling-Based Architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".serena/memories/jira-slack-integration-infrastructure.md", "source_location": "## 9. Webhook/Real-time Infrastructure", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No Jira webhooks, WebSockets, SSE, or Slack event subscriptions exist; the macOS app polls every 30s and cron checks run at minute precision. This keeps the system stateless on Vercel and means real-time upgrades can be added without breaking existing code."}, {"id": "memories_jira_slack_integration_infrastructure_lazyhandbar_polling", "label": "LazyhandBar Polling Orchestration (TicketListViewModel)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".serena/memories/jira-slack-integration-infrastructure.md", "source_location": "## 1. macOS App Polling Infrastructure", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Timer.scheduledTimer with configurable interval (default 30s from AppConfig.pollingInterval in ~/.lazyhand/config.json); detects new tickets by diffing fetched keys against a known set, then plays sound, shows banner, and updates the widget."}, {"id": "memories_jira_slack_integration_infrastructure_jira_service_client", "label": "Jira Service Client (lib/services/jira.ts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".serena/memories/jira-slack-integration-infrastructure.md", "source_location": "## 3. Backend Service Layer (Jira Integration)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Uses HTTP Basic Auth (email:apiToken base64) against Jira REST v3 (search/jql, comments, transitions, attachments); transformIssue maps custom fields customfield_10451/10453/10400 to wlMainTicketType/wlSubTicketType/customerLevel and merges saved status/action from the DB."}, {"id": "memories_jira_slack_integration_infrastructure_dynamic_cron_scheduling", "label": "Dynamic Trigger-Time Cron Scheduling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".serena/memories/jira-slack-integration-infrastructure.md", "source_location": "## 5. Scheduling & Cron Infrastructure", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Vercel only supports one hard-coded cron (daily backup), so /api/cron?task=shift is hit every minute and compares the current Asia/Bangkok time against trigger_time_1 (17:10) and trigger_time_2 (22:40) stored in the app_settings table \u2014 letting users change shift times without redeploying."}, {"id": "memories_jira_slack_integration_infrastructure_prisma_models", "label": "Prisma Data Models (TicketData/AppSetting/ScheduledComment/Backup)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".serena/memories/jira-slack-integration-infrastructure.md", "source_location": "## 6. Database Setup (PostgreSQL + Prisma)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "memories_jira_slack_integration_infrastructure_env_schema", "label": "Zod Environment Schema (lib/env.ts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".serena/memories/jira-slack-integration-infrastructure.md", "source_location": "## 7. Environment Configuration", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All env vars validated with Zod at startup (DATABASE_URL, JIRA_URL/EMAIL/API_TOKEN, SLACK_* tokens, GROQ/OPENAI keys, AI_PROVIDER default groq); getDatabaseConfig caps pool at 3 connections in prod for serverless."}], "edges": [{"source": "memories_jira_slack_integration_infrastructure_polling_architecture", "target": "memories_jira_slack_integration_infrastructure_lazyhandbar_polling", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".serena/memories/jira-slack-integration-infrastructure.md", "source_location": "## 9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source"